{{!< default}}
{{#contentFor "moHead"}}
<title>Compare | The Faith Received</title>
<meta name="description" content="Set two to four authors side by side on one topic. Now the Compare tab of the Research desk." />
{{!-- The Research page is the one that should rank. Two URLs for one
     workspace is a duplicate, and this is the copy that is only here to
     forward. --}}
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow" />
<link rel="canonical" href="https://mereorthodoxy.com/the-faith-received/research/" />
{{/contentFor}}
{{!-- /the-faith-received/compare/ — a redirect into the Research desk.

     WHAT HAPPENED. Compare was a page. It is now the Compare tab of
     /the-faith-received/research/, along with the Desk, and Pins is the
     collection strip inside that page's Notebook tab. This template is
     what is left of the old page: no markup, no scripts, no styles, one
     job.

     WHY THIS URL STILL EXISTS AT ALL. Because Compare puts its entire
     view in the address — #a=<authors>&sel=<topic>&g=&s=&q= — which is
     the thing that makes a comparison shareable and is the reason
     anybody has ever pasted one of these links anywhere. If this route
     404'd, every comparison anyone has shared would die, and it would
     die silently: a 404 does not tell the reader that the thing they
     were sent still exists somewhere else. The saved comparisons in
     readers' own browsers are stored as these addresses too.

     WHY IT IS A CLIENT-SIDE REDIRECT AND NOT A SERVER ONE. The state is
     in the FRAGMENT, and a fragment never reaches the server. A 301 in
     routes.yaml could send /compare/ to /research/ but could not turn
     #a=x into #compare&a=x, and the Research page would read a bare
     #a=x as an unknown workspace and clamp to Ask — the comparison
     would be dropped on the floor while the reader was told nothing.
     Only a script that can see the fragment can carry it across, so
     the transform happens here. It also means routes.yaml does not have
     to change, which matters: it is uploaded by hand in Ghost Admin and
     is not free.

     THE TRANSFORM. The Research page's hash is `#<mode>` followed by
     the panel's own state after the first "&" (the grammar is set out
     at the top of assets/js/page/faith-research.js). So:

       /the-faith-received/compare/                 -> /research/#compare
       /the-faith-received/compare/#a=x,y&sel=sin   -> /research/#compare&a=x,y&sel=sin

     location.replace, not assign: this page must not sit in the back
     stack, or Back from the Research desk would bounce the reader
     through here and straight forward again.

     WITHOUT SCRIPT there is a real link, and it is the whole content of
     the page rather than a hidden fallback. A redirect that only works
     with JavaScript is a dead end for anything that does not run it,
     and that includes the crawler that has to be told where this went. --}}

<main class="faith-received faith-feature">
  <section class="bhero bhero--tool">
    <div class="bhero-inner container">
      <p class="bhero-kicker"><a href="/the-faith-received/">The Faith Received</a></p>
      <h1>Compare has moved</h1>
      <p class="bhero-sub">Compare is now a tab of the Research desk, beside Ask, Power Search and the rest. This link still works, it just takes a moment longer.</p>
      <p class="bhero-sub"><a href="/the-faith-received/research/#compare" data-cmp-forward>Open Compare on the Research desk</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<script>
  (function () {
    // The old address kept its state in the fragment; the new one keeps
    // the same state after a mode segment. Anything that is not ours
    // (an empty hash, or "#compare" already) still lands on the tab.
    var hash = String(window.location.hash || "").replace(/^#/, "");
    var target = "/the-faith-received/research/#compare" + (hash && hash !== "compare" ? "&" + hash : "");

    // The link is corrected before the redirect fires, so that a reader
    // whose navigation is blocked or slow still has the right one under
    // the cursor.
    var a = document.querySelector("[data-cmp-forward]");
    if (a) a.setAttribute("href", target);

    window.location.replace(target);
  })();
</script>
